    "coverImage": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Havelock%2C_Andaman_%26_Nicobar_Islands.JPG/1280px-Havelock%2C_Andaman_%26_Nicobar_Islands.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail",
    "description": "Renowned for Radhanagar’s silver sands and mystical mangrove canals where marine life and ancient island myths thrive in unspoiled harmony.",
    "longDescription": "Swaraj Dweep was long regarded by ancient Asian mariners as an enchanted isle where the sea-winds sing in harmony with the tides. The dense mangrove channels were believed to be portals to the underwater realm of the Nagas, where water-borne spirits weave bioluminescent threads that make the midnight lagoons glitter like liquid diamonds.\n\nHistorically home to indigenous Great Andamanese clans before colonization, the island was later renamed Swaraj Dweep to honor Netaji Subhash Chandra Bose hoisting the first Indian flag on Andaman soil in 1943. Today, its lush interior jungle hides ancient hardwood padauk trees and vibrant elephant swimming traditions.\n\nSwaraj Dweep invites wanderers to step into living chapters of sacred lore and timeless folklore in Andaman and Nicobar Islands.",
    "loreTitle": "The Kingdom of Ocean Walkers & Glowing Lagoons",
    "ancientLegend": "Swaraj Dweep was long regarded by ancient Asian mariners as an enchanted isle where the sea-winds sing in harmony with the tides. The dense mangrove channels were believed to be portals to the underwater realm of the Nagas, where water-borne spirits weave bioluminescent threads that make the midnight lagoons glitter like liquid diamonds.",
    "historicalChronicle": "Historically home to indigenous Great Andamanese clans before colonization, the island was later renamed Swaraj Dweep to honor Netaji Subhash Chandra Bose hoisting the first Indian flag on Andaman soil in 1943. Today, its lush interior jungle hides ancient hardwood padauk trees and vibrant elephant swimming traditions.",
    "folkloreTales": [
      "The Starlight Kayak Phenomenon: Paddling into the mangrove channels on a moonless night awakens glowing swirls of blue plankton—believed by locals to be the laughter of sea nymphs.",
      "The Elephant of the Ocean: Local lore remembers the legendary swimming elephant Rajan, who was said to possess the blessing of Lord Ganesha to traverse the deep open ocean safely."
    ],
