    "coverImage": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/Rajgir_-_046_Side_View_%289242059259%29.jpg/1280px-Rajgir_-_046_Side_View_%289242059259%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail",
    "description": "Encircled by five majestic hills, Rajgir was the ancient capital of Magadha where Buddha turned the second wheel of Dhamma and Mahavira spent years in meditation.",
    "longDescription": "Perched on Griddhakuta (Vulture Peak), Lord Buddha delivered some of his most profound discourses, including the Heart Sutra and the Lotus Sutra. Nearby lies Saptaparni Cave, where 500 enlightened Arhats gathered just months after the Buddha’s Mahaparinirvana to recite and preserve the entire Buddhist canon for future millennia.\n\nKing Bimbisara and his son Ajatashatru fortified Rajgir with massive cyclopean stone walls spanning over 40 kilometers along the mountain ridges—constructed from raw uncut boulders that predate classical Greek and Roman fortifications.\n\nRajgir invites wanderers to step into living chapters of sacred lore and timeless folklore in Bihar.",
    "loreTitle": "The Vulture Peak & The Gold Vault of King Bimbisara",
    "ancientLegend": "Perched on Griddhakuta (Vulture Peak), Lord Buddha delivered some of his most profound discourses, including the Heart Sutra and the Lotus Sutra. Nearby lies Saptaparni Cave, where 500 enlightened Arhats gathered just months after the Buddha’s Mahaparinirvana to recite and preserve the entire Buddhist canon for future millennia.",
    "historicalChronicle": "King Bimbisara and his son Ajatashatru fortified Rajgir with massive cyclopean stone walls spanning over 40 kilometers along the mountain ridges—constructed from raw uncut boulders that predate classical Greek and Roman fortifications.",
    "folkloreTales": [
      "The Sonbhandar Gold Treasury: Legend says the cave of Sonbhandar was the royal treasury of King Bimbisara. An undeciphered inscription in Sankhalipi script on the cave wall is said to contain the secret password to open the solid stone door hiding thousands of tons of ancient gold.",
      "The Healing Brahmakund: The natural hot sulphur springs at the foot of Vaibhava Hill are believed to be heated by subterranean fires stoked by ascetic rishis."
    ],
