    "description": "A peaceful sanctuary of crescent beaches, heritage Portuguese mansions, and ancient prehistoric rock art nestled between the Arabian Sea and the Western Ghats.",
    "longDescription": "Local Konkan fisherfolk believe South Goa’s sheltered bays were blessed by Goddess Shantadurga, the mediator goddess who intervened to end the ferocious battle between Lord Shiva and Lord Vishnu by taking them both onto her lap in cosmic reconciliation.\n\nSouth Goa preserves some of India’s oldest archaeological wonders, including the 10,000-year-old Mesolithic rock petroglyphs at Usgalimal along the banks of the Kushavati River. In Chandor, the ancient capital of the Kadamba dynasty, grand 400-year-old mansions like the Braganza House showcase rare rosewood furniture, Belgian crystal chandeliers, and secret priest-holes.\n\nSouth Goa invites wanderers to step into living chapters of sacred lore and timeless folklore in Goa.",
    "loreTitle": "The Butterfly Bay of Palolem & The Rock Carvings of Usgalimal",
