    "coverImage": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Sri_Ranganathaswami_Temple%2C_Srirangaptna.jpg/1280px-Sri_Ranganathaswami_Temple%2C_Srirangaptna.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail",
    "description": "An island fortress enclosed by the Cauvery River, Srirangapatna was the capital of Hyder Ali and Tipu Sultan (\"The Tiger of Mysore\"), renowned for the Adi Ranga shrine and medieval battlements.",
    "longDescription": "The island has been sacred since Vedic times as the foremost of the three sacred islands of Lord Ranganatha (Sri Ranganathaswamy) along the Cauvery River. Sage Gautama performed intense penance here to receive a vision of Lord Vishnu reclining on the coils of serpent Adisesha.\n\nSrirangapatna was transformed by Tipu Sultan into an unbreachable fortress armed with military rocket artillery (the Mysorean rockets, the world’s first iron-cased artillery rockets). In May 1799, the British under General Harris breached the water gate after a long siege; Tipu Sultan died sword in hand defending his island citadel.\n\nSrirangapatna invites wanderers to step into living chapters of sacred lore and timeless folklore in Karnataka.",
    "loreTitle": "The Battlements of Tipu Sultan & The Ranganathaswamy Island",
    "ancientLegend": "The island has been sacred since Vedic times as the foremost of the three sacred islands of Lord Ranganatha (Sri Ranganathaswamy) along the Cauvery River. Sage Gautama performed intense penance here to receive a vision of Lord Vishnu reclining on the coils of serpent Adisesha.",
    "historicalChronicle": "Srirangapatna was transformed by Tipu Sultan into an unbreachable fortress armed with military rocket artillery (the Mysorean rockets, the world’s first iron-cased artillery rockets). In May 1799, the British under General Harris breached the water gate after a long siege; Tipu Sultan died sword in hand defending his island citadel.",
    "folkloreTales": [
      "The Dungeon of Colonel Bailey: The subterranean riverfront dungeon where British officers were imprisoned still has the rusted iron wall-clamps where prisoners were chained in river floodwaters.",
      "The Teak Frescoes of Dariya Daulat Bagh: Tipu Sultan’s summer palace is constructed entirely of seasoned teakwood, its interior walls covered in vivid frescoes depicting the Battle of Pollilur using natural mineral paints."
    ],
