    "coverImage": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Pachmarhi_valley_Madhya_Pradesh_INDIA.jpg/1280px-Pachmarhi_valley_Madhya_Pradesh_INDIA.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail",
    "description": "The only hill station in Madhya Pradesh, Pachmarhi (\"Queen of the Satpuras\") is a verdant plateau of waterfalls, deep ravines, sal forests, and prehistoric cave paintings.",
    "longDescription": "According to the Mahabharata, the five Pandava brothers and Draupadi spent a year of their exile living in the sandstone caves atop Pachmarhi hill, which gave the town its name (Panch-Marhi, \"Five Caves\"). Nearby stands the colossal 300-foot sheer gorge of Handi Khoh, where local tribal legend says Lord Shiva imprisoned a venomous demon serpent in a deep pit.\n\nRediscovered in 1857 by British Army Captain James Forsyth while leading a cavalry patrol, Pachmarhi was developed as a cantonment sanatorium. The plateau is famous for perennial waterfalls like Bee Falls, Duchess Falls, and Silver Falls (Rajat Prapat), which plunges 350 feet like a single ribbon of silver milk.\n\nPachmarhi invites wanderers to step into living chapters of sacred lore and timeless folklore in Madhya Pradesh.",
    "loreTitle": "The Caves of the Pandavas & The Chasm of Handi Khoh",
    "ancientLegend": "According to the Mahabharata, the five Pandava brothers and Draupadi spent a year of their exile living in the sandstone caves atop Pachmarhi hill, which gave the town its name (Panch-Marhi, \"Five Caves\"). Nearby stands the colossal 300-foot sheer gorge of Handi Khoh, where local tribal legend says Lord Shiva imprisoned a venomous demon serpent in a deep pit.",
    "historicalChronicle": "Rediscovered in 1857 by British Army Captain James Forsyth while leading a cavalry patrol, Pachmarhi was developed as a cantonment sanatorium. The plateau is famous for perennial waterfalls like Bee Falls, Duchess Falls, and Silver Falls (Rajat Prapat), which plunges 350 feet like a single ribbon of silver milk.",
    "folkloreTales": [
      "The Sunset on Dhoopgarh: Dhoopgarh (4,429 ft) is the highest point in Madhya Pradesh and the entire Satpura Range, offering 360-degree sunset panoramas where the sun dips into a sea of endless sal canopy.",
      "The Sacred Cave of Jata Shankar: Inside a dark natural limestone cave, rock stalactites and freshwater springs resemble the matted locks (Jata) of Lord Shiva, where wild bees nest undisturbed."
    ],
