    "coverImage": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/Qila_Mubarak%2C_Patiala.jpg/1280px-Qila_Mubarak%2C_Patiala.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail",
    "description": "The princely heartland of the Phulkian dynasty, celebrated for the 18th-century Qila Mubarak fortress, vibrant Phulkari floral silk embroideries, and opulent royal lifestyle lore.",
    "longDescription": "Founded in 1763 by Baba Ala Singh of the Sidhu Jat Sikh clan, Patiala’s foundation was blessed by the sword of Guru Gobind Singh. The name derives from \"Pati-Ala\" (\"The Estate of Ala\"). The royal court became renowned across the subcontinent for its generous patronage of classical Hindustani music, giving rise to the prestigious Patiala Gharana.\n\nThe 10-acre Qila Mubarak palace complex features the Sheesh Mahal (Palace of Mirrors) decorated with Kangra and Rajasthani miniature frescoes and a colossal collection of European chandeliers. Maharaja Bhupinder Singh was one of the 20th century’s most flamboyant monarchs, commissioning the famous 1928 \"Patiala Necklace\" from Cartier containing 2,930 diamonds.\n\nPatiala invites wanderers to step into living chapters of sacred lore and timeless folklore in Punjab.",
    "loreTitle": "The Mud Fortress of Ala Singh & The World’s Largest Diamond Necklace",
    "ancientLegend": "Founded in 1763 by Baba Ala Singh of the Sidhu Jat Sikh clan, Patiala’s foundation was blessed by the sword of Guru Gobind Singh. The name derives from \"Pati-Ala\" (\"The Estate of Ala\"). The royal court became renowned across the subcontinent for its generous patronage of classical Hindustani music, giving rise to the prestigious Patiala Gharana.",
    "historicalChronicle": "The 10-acre Qila Mubarak palace complex features the Sheesh Mahal (Palace of Mirrors) decorated with Kangra and Rajasthani miniature frescoes and a colossal collection of European chandeliers. Maharaja Bhupinder Singh was one of the 20th century’s most flamboyant monarchs, commissioning the famous 1928 \"Patiala Necklace\" from Cartier containing 2,930 diamonds.",
    "folkloreTales": [
      "The Legend of the Patiala Peg: The legendary 120ml liquor measurement \"Patiala Peg\" originated during a friendly polo match hosted by Maharaja Bhupinder Singh against the British Viceroy’s team, where oversized drinks were poured to slow the rivals down.",
      "The Sacred Joti of Qila Mubarak: In the heart of the inner fortress (Qila Androon) burns the Akhand Dhuni (Eternal Fire), lit by Baba Ala Singh from the embers of saintly wood over 260 years ago and tended continuously by royal caretakers."
    ],
