    "coverImage": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/India_Bikaner_Junagarh_Fort.jpg/1280px-India_Bikaner_Junagarh_Fort.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail",
    "description": "Founded in 1488 by Rao Bika amidst golden desert sands, Bikaner is celebrated for the unassailable Junagarh Fort, spicy Bikaneri Bhujia, and the unique Karni Mata Temple at Deshnoke.",
    "longDescription": "Rao Bika, a Rathore prince of Jodhpur, rode into the wilderness of the Thar desert after his father jokingly remarked that he was whispering plans to build his own kingdom. Guided by the blessings of the female warrior-sage Karni Mata, he founded an unbreachable desert empire that was never conquered by outside invaders.\n\nUnlike most Rajasthani forts built on hills, Junagarh Fort is built directly on the desert plains. It contains opulent palaces like Anup Mahal with gold leaf lacquer ceilings and Badal Mahal painted with blue monsoon clouds. At Deshnoke, 25,000 sacred black rats (Kabbas) roam freely inside the silver-doored temple of Karni Mata.\n\nBikaner invites wanderers to step into living chapters of sacred lore and timeless folklore in Rajasthan.",
    "loreTitle": "The Desert Bastions of Junagarh & The 25,000 Sacred Rats of Deshnoke",
    "ancientLegend": "Rao Bika, a Rathore prince of Jodhpur, rode into the wilderness of the Thar desert after his father jokingly remarked that he was whispering plans to build his own kingdom. Guided by the blessings of the female warrior-sage Karni Mata, he founded an unbreachable desert empire that was never conquered by outside invaders.",
    "historicalChronicle": "Unlike most Rajasthani forts built on hills, Junagarh Fort is built directly on the desert plains. It contains opulent palaces like Anup Mahal with gold leaf lacquer ceilings and Badal Mahal painted with blue monsoon clouds. At Deshnoke, 25,000 sacred black rats (Kabbas) roam freely inside the silver-doored temple of Karni Mata.",
    "folkloreTales": [
      "The Sighting of the White Kabba: Seeing one of the four rare white rats among the 25,000 black rats at Karni Mata Temple is considered an omen of supreme fortune and divine blessing.",
      "The Bikaneri Bhujia Heritage: Made from moth bean flour and desert spices fried in groundnut oil, Bikaner produces over 50,000 kilograms of its GI-tagged crunchy bhujia every day."
    ],
