    "coverImage": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/Kanchenjunga_range_from_tea_gardens_of_darjeeling.jpg/1280px-Kanchenjunga_range_from_tea_gardens_of_darjeeling.jpg",
    "description": "Perched at 6,700 feet amidst rolling emerald tea estates and pine ridges, Darjeeling is world-famous for \"Champagne of Teas\", the UNESCO-listed Himalayan Railway, and Tiger Hill sunrises.",
    "longDescription": "The name Darjeeling is derived from the Tibetan words \"Dorje\" (Thunderbolt) and \"Ling\" (Place) — \"The Land of the Cosmic Thunderbolt\". Sages revere Observatory Hill as the sacred abode of Mahakala, where a Buddhist monastery and Hindu shrine share the same sacred hilltop covered in colorful prayer flags.\n\nDeveloped in the 19th century as a British sanatorium, Darjeeling produces the world’s most coveted high-altitude Muscatel black tea. The Darjeeling Himalayan Railway (the \"Toy Train\"), opened in 1881, uses vintage B-class steam locomotives to climb the zigzag loops of Batasia Loop and Ghoom (India’s highest railway station at 7,407 ft).\n\nDarjeeling invites wanderers to step into living chapters of sacred lore and timeless folklore in West Bengal.",
    "loreTitle": "The Thunderbolt Hill of Dorje Ling & The Sunrise of Tiger Hill",
    "ancientLegend": "The name Darjeeling is derived from the Tibetan words \"Dorje\" (Thunderbolt) and \"Ling\" (Place) — \"The Land of the Cosmic Thunderbolt\". Sages revere Observatory Hill as the sacred abode of Mahakala, where a Buddhist monastery and Hindu shrine share the same sacred hilltop covered in colorful prayer flags.",
    "historicalChronicle": "Developed in the 19th century as a British sanatorium, Darjeeling produces the world’s most coveted high-altitude Muscatel black tea. The Darjeeling Himalayan Railway (the \"Toy Train\"), opened in 1881, uses vintage B-class steam locomotives to climb the zigzag loops of Batasia Loop and Ghoom (India’s highest railway station at 7,407 ft).",
    "folkloreTales": [
      "The Tiger Hill Sunrise Miracle: At 4:00 AM, thousands gather at Tiger Hill (8,482 ft) to watch the first rays of dawn illuminate the snow peak of Mount Kanchenjunga in dazzling shades of gold, pink, and incandescent amber.",
      "The Legend of Tenzing Norgay: The Himalayan Mountaineering Institute houses the legacy of Sherpa Tenzing Norgay, who with Sir Edmund Hillary made the first historic summit of Mount Everest in 1953."
    ],
